## Tooling conventions

{% if language == "python" %}
### Quality checks use pre-commit

Top-level `.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs the relevant tools.
Install and run with:

```bash
uvx pre-commit install
uvx pre-commit run --all-files
```

{% if github_remote %}
The same checks run in GitHub Actions via
`.github/workflows/quality.yml`.
{% endif %}

### Python toolchain

| Concern                   | Tool         | Source             |
|---------------------------|--------------|--------------------|
| Project / package manager | `uv`         | Astral             |
| Build backend             | `uv_build`   | Astral             |
| Linter + formatter        | `ruff`       | Astral             |
| Type checker              | `ty`         | Astral             |
| Test runner               | `pytest`     | pytest project     |
| Pre-commit framework      | `pre-commit` | pre-commit project |

Default principle: if Astral ships a tool for the concern, use it.
Pick a mature alternative only when Astral has no coverage
(currently: test runner, pre-commit framework).

### Python sub-projects use their own `uv` project

Each Python-based sub-project (`dev-tools/queue/` is the bundled
example) manages tooling locally via `uv` — `pyproject.toml` +
`uv.lock` — and runs via `uv run --directory <subproject> ...`.
Don't depend on globally-installed `pip`, `pipx`, or `uv tool`
unless the tool is explicitly user-global.

### Python style

Imports at module top per PEP 8. Inline imports inside a function
are acceptable only for a functional reason (breaking a circular
import, deferring an optional or heavy dependency, working around a
load-order constraint). "I added it where I needed it" is not a
functional reason; lift it.
{% else %}
### Quality checks

This cell is language-agnostic. Add the appropriate quality tooling
when you commit to a primary language: linter, formatter, test
runner, type checker. The bundled queue under `dev-tools/queue/`
brings its own Python toolchain via `uv` regardless of the cell's
primary language.
{% endif %}

